a81_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;via Instagram &lt;a href="http://bit.ly/2j6JLyK" rel="nofollow"&gt;bit.ly/2j6JLyK&lt;/a&gt; January 23, 2017 at 08:43PM http://flic.kr/p/RgrTym, January 23, 2017 at 08:43PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sunset clouds</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sunset-clouds/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Oct 2016 08:53:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sunset-clouds/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://farm6.staticflickr.com/5602/29982923974_32b89019f2_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;http://flic.kr/p/MFujH5, October 27, 2016 at 06:46PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 102, post gym session</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-102-post-gym-session/</link><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jul 2013 19:22:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-102-post-gym-session/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; the only link in this post is now broken. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7416/9239886413_862c840282_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Sun going down after a good gym session. http://flic.kr/p/f5uQjr, July 08, 2013 at 08:58PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sunset in Ripon</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sunset-in-ripon/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Apr 2013 11:37:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sunset-in-ripon/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm9.staticflickr.com/8537/8667242485_441925610b_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;View from the back door. http://flic.kr/p/ecTTeg, April 20, 2013 at 09:09PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Experiments in HDR</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/experiments-in-hdr/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jul 2010 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/experiments-in-hdr/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is my first real attempt at an HDR image, taken from three shot with a 1.3+- exposure bracketing.&lt;br /&gt;The foreground is a bit blurry as the wind was moving the plants and I wasn&amp;rsquo;t using a tripod, notes for next time.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4776720007/" title="Ripon Sunset HDR by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4102/4776720007_2035ce11c9.jpg" width="500" height="342" alt="Ripon Sunset HDR" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;After converting from the RAW files I arranged the three images as separate layers in Photoshop.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;The layers where arranged as +1.3 exposure,normal,-1.3.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Then I added layer masks to the top two layers.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Painting on the top layer mask I removed the &amp;ldquo;burnt out&amp;rdquo; sections from the top layers so the correctly exposed section from the layer below showed through.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;I repeated this again on the second layer.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;I ran a low Gaussian blur on the layer masks to soften the edges of the masks to reduce the halo effect.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Then I merge each layer into the one below to create the finished image.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alastair Montgomery&amp;rsquo;s Photography&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>April Ripon Sunset</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/april-ripon-sunset/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2009 09:36:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/april-ripon-sunset/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3465366398/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3540/3465366398_ef6f6bf0c1_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style=" margin-top: 0px;font-size:0.9em;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3465366398/"&gt;April Ripon Sunset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;p&gt;Taken on my LG RENOIR KC910 when walking the dog on Hells Wath Ripon&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Picture : leaving work sunset.</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/picture-leaving-work-sunset/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 10:06:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/picture-leaving-work-sunset/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg2p-gg4S-UiUQvne32bbbxP2qKkbnS6A6VQHM4mtbiWq3YbKOeSeuC_tY2k9LT-ZRMMyoZSsa4M2WrAGyggbg_jcADXwxFECVaPOKMCMSqpfurtSCoOC2fJcKv-wfttqePVHEK/s1600-h/image-upload-42-792336.jpg"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg2p-gg4S-UiUQvne32bbbxP2qKkbnS6A6VQHM4mtbiWq3YbKOeSeuC_tY2k9LT-ZRMMyoZSsa4M2WrAGyggbg_jcADXwxFECVaPOKMCMSqpfurtSCoOC2fJcKv-wfttqePVHEK/s400/image-upload-42-792336.jpg"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span&gt;Snapped this sunset in York on my phone, leaving work yesterday.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Pink sky at night</title><link>https://bl